data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span` of native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

The test confirmed correct allocation, indexing, and values. On this 64-bit system, `nint`/`nuint` are 8 bytes each. The only gotcha: `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't predefined (it varies by platform).
